  "id": "reactivation-of-memory",
  "term": "reactivation of memory",
  "definition": "Reactivation of memory is the bringing back into activity of stored memory traces so that past experiences can be recalled again. In this source, it refers to repetition helping revive autobiographical memories, even in people with severe amnesia related to Alzheimer disease.",
